/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090323 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bc02d67b-661f-5114-b99b-4fecf9959b21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090324 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{5}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090324 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090324 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d7636b6-14d7-5113-bee3-f346d2f16556" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090325 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090325 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090325 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e27ec4d-090a-570a-b5c5-10c16ab97587" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090326 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090326 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090326 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3050e6c6-6028-5716-983d-b12f2b71e0f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090327 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090327 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186090327 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4651dfd7-c459-57b1-a12c-fef1de09aa88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092078 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5483" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092078 #edb/ref 1071 "Find an eigenvector of ![](images/39/398028421c4e26ae608c211073d010cfd7860476cec0861cb986bcc7a9cc91af.svg)\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\,\\lambda=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092078 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ea5361d-2508-5d54-acbf-46a57be601f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092078 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,\\lambda =2.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). So, $x_2$ is a free variable. \n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n5x_1-4x_2=0\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx_1=\\dfrac{4}{5}x_2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n![](images/10/105c85a9f0f6bc92ac8f062d52790babc3331db1283bf4380fad442418d870eb.svg)\n\nFinally, setting $x_2=5,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n![](images/82/82cec52e485c08116a7e07f4b9d5b01355e8bebdd4fb910535a001e5e979a099.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092079 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092079 #edb/ref 1071 "If ![](images/38/38d451c4fe8eff5b96fe2df730315c129fac48c05324c8603576a69898665e54.svg) is an eigenvector of ![](images/57/576b0cfcb7e902b8fcb9c98d25a2145f760618d9a56ed257f4828d6ab3b05064.svg)\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\,\\lambda=1$, then what is the value of $\\,\\dfrac{b}{a}\\,?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f23dcdbe-03e6-582f-8383-b07a1b2036c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092079 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,\\lambda =1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). So, $x_2$ is a free variable. \n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\nx_1+5x_2=0\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx_1=-5x_2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n![](images/1e/1e196ae1de5d8582ec93c6f964187b9b2b85b54f3b23e4017e50a1545310348c.svg)\n\nSetting, for instance, $x_2=-1,$ we get the following eigenvector:\n\n![](images/67/67e700524b8c7acc8923fd97acd1bb77b391944b91c891e4ce9388b22575709b.svg)\n\nFinally, $\\dfrac{b}{a}=\\dfrac{-1}{5}=-\\dfrac{1}{5}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092080 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092080 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $\\lambda=1$ and $\\lambda=-4$ are the eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](images/b1/b1b6bc95f7d29e0c64007e7c19a4690eb3def3e58d677d8a21604315bbb21c0a.svg)\nfind two linearly independent eigenvectors of $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092080 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b59a8ad2-7233-54c2-9055-5e188e0b8503" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092080 #edb/ref 1074 "We can get two linearly independent eigenvectors by simply finding eigenvectors corresponding to the different eigenvalues.\n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the eigenvalues separately. \n\n- For $\\lambda =1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]-1[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have to solve the corresponding system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $2$nd one). So, $x_1$ is a free variable. \nFrom the first equation, we obtain  $x_2=0.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n![](images/81/812c2f9dfcb3943cc13c47d2f1b85d9b1a67ce10c9e6a965a9bb915655d0316c.svg)\nSetting, for instance, $x_1=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n![](images/7d/7d3a9e02893b98a2739398d48138be4c930ea87b3e3577776cfdd7edf6faf4e7.svg)\n\n- For $\\lambda =-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]-(-4)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have to solve the corresponding system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). So, $x_2$ is a free variable. \nFrom the first equation, we obtain $x_1=\\dfrac{1}{5}x_2.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n![](images/ea/ea5ff5d281eb5376520b2763f8dd96a926d52b6485452dd60b741b48ad0d7def.svg)\nSetting, for instance, $x_2=5,$ we get the eigenvector \n![](images/db/db85af375c67eca1f1d197a284b99ef7baf9fdb543b376c27e02c3d837742b68.svg)\n\nTherefore, two linearly independent eigenvectors of the matrix $A$